From 31637fba65186f7ab8b864e090666aeb34ba402f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mokomis <24596443+Mokomis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:12:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] diag(pyrowave): replay a capture and dump raw decoded planes
 per driver

For the Turnip vs Qualcomm comparison on the OPPO Pad Mini: decode the same
captured AUs on either driver and compare the raw Y/Cb/Cr planes before any
colour conversion or presentation.

- pyrowave_planes example: decodes a PUNKTFUNK_DUMP_VIDEO capture and writes
  each frame's planes plus a manifest with the driver identity and SHA-256 per
  plane. PYROWAVE_ICD loads a driver by path (as AdrenoTools does);
  PYROWAVE_PLANES_IDWT forces the inverse-wavelet path; PYROWAVE_PRECISION
  passes through. Runs on Linux, Windows and Android.
- pyrowave_compare_planes.py: per plane, identical or how and where it
  differs (codes, PSNR, 32x32 tiles, edge tiles), with optional diff images.
- Android capture: setprop debug.punktfunk.dump_video <dir> records up to
  debug.punktfunk.dump_video_frames AUs (default 240) and a mode.txt.
- Decoder: frames expose all three plane images; set_plane_readback adds
  TRANSFER_SRC to plane images, off unless a test turns it on.
